# <node-number> host=<address> role=validator|rpc|pchain|archive [chain=<name>] [weight=<n>] [dc=<tag>]
# Validators are registered in ascending node-number order. The default
# ladder: the first three validators OF EACH CHAIN start at weight 100000;
# every remaining validator starts at 1000.
# weight= overrides the ladder with an explicit initial stake (an integer,
# at least 1). It is valid only on validator lines.
# Set it on every validator of a chain or on none; a mix is an error.
# chain= names the L1 a node serves (lowercase letters, digits, hyphens; at
# most 20 characters). Omitted means main. Every named chain needs at least
# one validator. The name management is reserved. See
# examples/two-chains.ini and playbooks/09-multi-chain.md.
# Exactly one pchain node hosts the P-chain beacon the fleet deploys through.
# It serves every chain and takes no chain= tag.
# archive nodes serve their chain with pruning and state-sync disabled; they
# must exist from genesis because an archive cannot state-sync. A single
# archive prints a warning: it cannot cross-check its answers.
# chain=oracle on validator and rpc lines declares the optional oracle L1;
# omit those lines to run without one. The legacy spellings oracle-validator
# and oracle-rpc still load and mean the same. Multiple nodes may share one
# host.
1  host=10.0.0.11 role=validator dc=A
2  host=10.0.0.12 role=validator dc=A
3  host=10.0.0.13 role=validator dc=A
4  host=10.0.0.14 role=validator dc=A
5  host=10.1.0.11 role=validator dc=B
6  host=10.1.0.12 role=validator dc=B
7  host=10.1.0.13 role=validator dc=B
8  host=10.1.0.14 role=validator dc=B
9  host=10.0.0.15 role=rpc       dc=A
10 host=10.0.0.16 role=rpc       dc=A
11 host=10.1.0.15 role=rpc       dc=B
12 host=10.1.0.16 role=rpc       dc=B
13 host=10.2.0.10 role=pchain
14 host=10.0.0.17 role=archive   dc=A
15 host=10.1.0.17 role=archive   dc=B
16 host=10.0.0.18 role=validator chain=oracle dc=A
17 host=10.0.0.15 role=rpc       chain=oracle dc=A
